  strength so he kept pushing him to  explain how he became so strong that's  when we learned that even as a kid  yorichi could see into the transparent  world so he could anticipate his  opponent's movements based on the  positions of their bones the  contractions of their muscles and the  flow of their blood yorichi was also  born with exceptional strength and speed  and that is when michigatu came to a  startling conclusion all this time he  had pitied his younger brother but the  truth was that yorichi was actually far  superior to him now michikatsu worked  hard and he had talent so he definitely  got stronger but his progress was  negligible compared to the overpowering  natural talents of yorichi and even  though yorici wasn't interested in the  samurai life anymore after the  instructor told their father about  yurichi's incredible talent the father  suddenly changed his mind he now wanted  yorichi to take over as the head of the  family instead of michikatsu and  michikatsu was now forced to sleep in  that small isolated room where yorichi  had slept all this time worse yet  michikatsu was now to be sent to the  temple when he turned 10 instead of  yurichi which meant that michikatsu's  lifelong dream of becoming a samurai  would never come true but then one night  while michikatsu was lying in bed  yorichi came to him and told them that  their mother had died michikatsu was  shocked by this and he thought the death  must have been very sudden but yorichi  merely told them to ask her servant  about the details because he will now be  departing for the temple michikatsu is  confused by this since yurichi was no  longer being forced to go to the temple  but yurichi says that he just wanted to  say goodbye yorichi also said that he  will bring the wooden flute that  michikatsu had made for him so that he  could feel close to his older brother  wherever he goes michikotsu thought that  flute was a poorly made piece of junk  that couldn't even produce sounds  properly and he was surprised to see  orichi safeguarding it inside a cloth  and acting like it was some sort of  treasure yorichi then left for the  temple and michikatsu proceeded to read  his mother's journal as he read the  journal he learned that yorichi had  sensed that their father was planning to  designate him as the heir instead of  michikatsu so he left for the temple  earlier than expected that way their  father would have no choice but to stick  to the original plan and allow michika  to succeed him as the head of the family  michikatsu also realized that his mother  had been suffering from an illness for  years and that yurichi had sensed it  this illness affected the left side of  their mother's body so when yorichi was  clinging to that side he wasn't really  clinging instead he was supporting her  because her body had been weakened from  the illness and in that moment as he  realized that yorichi was so much more  observant and talented and compassionate  than him michikatsu began to burn with  jealousy it was like yorichi was perfect  in every way superior in every way and  in that moment michikatsu hated his own  brother from the bottom of his heart  because he was so profoundly jealous of  yorichi's genius the irony here is that  when yurichi was treated as the black  sheep of the family michikatsu felt  sorry for him and he tried to help him  but it is clear that in his own mind  michikatsu had also accepted the idea  that he was superior to yorichi when the  tables turned and yorichi was shown to  be far more impressive than his brother  in practically every way michikatsu's  ego couldn't handle it and he began  wishing that his brother had never been  born because his very existence defied  the laws of nature nevertheless  michikatsu's jealousy subsided after  yurichi disappeared from his life  although their father tried to bring  yurichi back from the temple yorichi had  disappeared without a trace and no one  could find him anywhere and so  michikachu's father had no choice but to  go back to the original plan michikatsu  was the heir apparent again and as 10  years passed he settled down and started  a family his days were tranquil and  boring and he lived a calm and  comfortable life but then one day a  demon attacked michikatsu and his men in  the forest the demon killed michikaw's  men and was about to kill him as well  when an adult yorichi showed up and took  the demon down in an instant the moment  that michikatsu saw his brother again he  could tell right away that yorichi had  mastered the sword and that he was an  incredible warrior michikatsu's serenity  was destroyed and he began to burn with  jealousy yet again yorichi was  unbelievably strong and he had an  impeccable character and michikatsu  decided that he would do anything to  become as strong and as skilled with a  sword as his brother so michikatsu  abandoned his family and he dedicated  his entire life to becoming a demon  slayer which was the same path that  yorichi had chosen michikatsu trained  directly under yurichi and he learned  breathing techniques directly from his  brother  but none of the demon slayers michikatsu  included were able to match yorichi's  power they simply could not replicate  the breathing style that he used the  breath of the sun so yorici changed the  breathing technique slightly as he  taught them to different individuals in  order to make it possible for them to  actually learn and master these  techniques that is how all the many  derivatives of sun breathing emerged and  one of those derivatives was  michikatsu's own moon breathing  eventually michikatsu manifested a  demonstrator mark identical to the one  that his twin brother was born with and  overall michikatsu became an extremely  strong swordsman and a top tier demon  slayer but despite his clearly  impressive strength he still couldn't  measure up to yorichi no matter how hard  he trained and no matter how much of his  life he dedicated to getting stronger  michikatsu could never learn sun  breathing and he could never compare to  the godlike skill and talent of his  brother to make things worse all the  demon players who managed to manifest  the demon sire mark began to die off  after reaching the age of 25 the demon  slayer mark bestowed the slayer with  more power but in exchange it  drastically shortened his lifespan  michikatsu realized that he was going to  die without ever even coming close to  achieving his dream of becoming the  strongest samurai and surpassing his  brother and that is when the notorious  demon king muzan approached him with a  proposal muzan told michikatsu that if  he became a demon he could live forever  and he wouldn't have to worry about  dying at the age of 25. he would have a  much stronger body and he would have all  of eternity to keep getting stronger  until his strength finally surpassed  even yorichi despite dedicating his  entire life to being a demon slayer and  destroying demons michikatsu's jealousy  and ego got the best of him he made a  deal with the devil he agreed to consume  muzan's blood and become a demon in  exchange for eternal life and superhuman  power afterwards michikatsu tsugikuni  became kokushibo and he turned against  his own demon slayer comrades together  with muzon he cut down the very demon  slayers that he had once called his  brethren so that no one would ever get  in the way of his and muzon's plans but  even after 60 years of being a demon  kokushibo still wasn't able to surpass  yorichi the two brothers would come face  to face again when yorichi was already  in his mid-80s naturally yorichi did not  die at the age of 25 despite having the  demon slayer mark which again emphasized  the fact that yorici was special and  more gifted than his brother being a  demon kokushiba didn't age and so he was  still at peak strength meanwhile yurichi  was a frail old man who inhabited a weak  human body instead of an immortal demon  body and yet even after six decades  yorichi was still stronger than  kokushibo his technique was so flawless  and godlike that he defeated the demon  kokushibo despite being an octogenarian  however yorichi died of old age before  he had the chance to strike the  finishing blow against kokushibo and so  kokushiba survived the battle but he was  forced to live another 400 years with  the knowledge that even as an old man  yurichi was still stronger than him to  make things worse when kokushibo cut  down yorichi's lifeless body he found  that small wooden flute that he had made  for his brother back when they were  children despite the fact that kokushibo  had betrayed the demonstr and despite  the fact that he became a ruthless demon  yorichi still carried that stupid crappy  flute that his twin brother gave him all  those years ago so not only was yorichi  stronger than kokushibo even in his 80s  but he still remained a man of flawless  character and endless compassion until  the very end as for kokushiba himself he  remained conflicted he was conflicted  between his love for his brother on the  one hand and his burning jealousy of him  on the other and he was also conflicted  between his lifelong desire to be an  honorable samurai warrior and the  reality of having become a demonic  monster these inner conflicts would  finally boil over during kokushiba's  final battle against muichiro genya  sanemi and gyome inside the infinity  castle the first opponent that kokushiba  encounters is the mist hashira muichiro  muichiro is immediately intimidated by  kokushibo's overpowering aura but  kokushiba's actual behavior is not what  you would expect from some blood thirsty  demon kokushibo is calm dignified and  polite and even asks for his opponent's  name before the battle begins once the  hashira introduces himself as muichiro  tokito kokushibo gives him his own human  name michikatsu  kuni kokushibo can sense that muichiro  is actually a descendant of one of the  children that he had left behind back  when he abandoned his family in order to  become a demon slayer the tsugikuni  family name must have died out over time  but muichiro was still a direct blood  descendant of kokushibo this is a  surprise to muichiro but it doesn't  change anything in terms of his own  goals and principles he steals his  nerves and attacks kokushibo with his  missed breathing techniques as muichiro  attempts to land a hit on kokushiba he  keeps missing over and over again but  kokushiba is still impressed with the  strength skill and courage of his  descendant especially since muichiro is  still only 14 years old kokushiba  decides that muichiro has earned his  respect and so he finally draws his  sword because not doing so would be  considered disrespectful towards his  opponent again notice that kokushibo  continues to cling to strict samurai  etiquette despite being a demon which  tells us that kokushibo has not given up  on his humanity at least not fully if  you pay close attention during his fight  you will also notice that kokushibo  doesn't like sustaining the kinds of  injuries that would kill a human even  though he clearly possesses demonic  regeneration he doesn't like having to  use it it's almost as if he considers  resorting to regeneration to be shameful  because if he had allowed himself to be  injured in that way as a human he would  have died as soon as kokushibo draws his  sword and reveals his moon breathing  technique muichiro is hit and loses his  hand but the young hashira is unfazed by  this he just uses his shirt to make a  tourniquet and continues to fight with  his other hand kokushibo is greatly  impressed by muijiro but more than just  being impressed by the actions of some  random stranger kokushibo is also proud  of his descendant he believes that  killing muichiro who is such a talented  warrior would be a shame and he decides  to ask muzan to turn muichiro into a  demon this is all important stuff  because you don't see someone like muzon  worrying about codes of honor samurai  etiquette or descendants muzon is  willing to do literally anything to stay  alive and satisfy his own desires and  all moral codes values and principles  are nothing to him so there is a stark  difference between kokushibo and muzon  in this regard kokushibo then pins  muichiro down to a pillar by piercing  him through the chest with his own sword  having immobilized his descendant  kokushibo plans to summon muzon and turn  muichiro into a demon however kokushibo  has to postpone this plan because he is  soon attacked by other demon slayers  first genya arrives and kokushibo takes  care of him pretty easily but then  sanemi and gyome also join the battle  and kokushiba is forced to turn his  attention to fighting the two hashida  muichiro uses the fact that kokushiba is  busy fighting gyome and sanemi to pull  the sword that had been pinning him to  the pillar from his own chest with his  own bare hands we can only imagine the  kind of pain that this caused him and  the insane amount of strength and  courage that was required for muichiro  to pull this off  say what you will about kokushi was  warped samurai values but he was  certainly right to be impressed by  muichiro at this point muichiro already  knows that he will almost certainly die  from blood loss as a result of the  injuries that he has already suffered  but he is determined to make a real  impact on the outcome of the battle  before he dies he jumps into the thick  of the battle and saves sanemy from one  of kokushiba's attacks and then  determined to help while he is still  able to move muichiro launches an  assault on kokushibo while kokushibu is  distracted by attacks from gyome and  tsunemi muichiro manages to move close  enough to pierce kokushibo's torso with  his sword muichiro loses one of his legs  during this approach but that doesn't  matter to him he is willing to make the  ultimate sacrifice in order to win this  battle as the epic battle rages muichiro  is determined to protect gyome and  tsunemi so that they will survive and be  able to continue to fight in the battle  against muzon he is so determined to  help defeat kokushiba before he dies  that his nichiren blade suddenly turns  red and this causes such pain to  kokushibo that he is unable to move  don't forget that red nichiren blades  can burn demons on a cellular level  which drastically reduces their ability  to regenerate a dying genya then manages  to use his blood demon art to keep  kokushibo in place long enough for  sunemi and gyome to take off his head  but even the loss of his head isn't  enough to take down a demon of  kokushibo's caliber as the demon slayers  look on in shock upper moon 1 is able to  regenerate even his head  but this second head looks nothing like  a human head it is a monstrous demonic  head and when kokushibo catches a  glimpse of his own face he is stunned  and disgusted and that is when the inner  conflict between kokushiba's deeply held  samurai values and the reality of being  a demon finally come to a head  ever since he was a child kokushiba  wanted to become the strongest samurai  in the world but after many years of  trying his best he eventually realized  that he could never surpass his  incredibly talented twin brother yorichi  yorichi had almost supernatural godlike  talent that simply could not be  surpassed  and so despite the fact that kokushiba  was an incredibly strong swordsman back  when he was human perhaps even the  second strongest swordsman in the world  after yurichi he was never quite good  enough to compete with his brother all  his training and dedication certainly  bore fruit and he became an unbelievable  warrior but there was just no way for  him to ever compare to yurichi kokushiba  tried everything to catch up to his  brother he abandoned his family he  betrayed his comrades and he gave up his  very humanity to surpass his brother and  to avoid defeat but in the end even a  deal with the devil himself didn't allow  him to achieve his dream not only did he  still fail to defeat yurichi but he also  failed to fulfill his initial dream the  one he had before becoming jealous of  his brother the dream of becoming the  strongest samurai upon seeing his  reflection kokushiba realized that even  if he had succeeded in becoming stronger  than yurichi once he became a demon he  would still not be the strongest samurai  that is because asamura lives by a code  of honor a samurai has values that he  would never abandon and a samurai would  rather die than live dishonorably a true  samurai would never willingly choose to  become a demon just to avoid accepting  defeat a true samurai would never devour  innocent people just to get stronger and  a true samurai doesn't have the face and  body of a monster kokushibo can't  believe that he allowed his fear of  defeat to turn him into an inhuman  creature kokushiba's internal conflicts  reach a boiling point he experiences a  severe crisis of conscience and his body  begins to break apart in the place where  muichiro had stabbed him with his red  blade kokushibo is then finished off by  gyome and sanemi and then after nearly  500 years of life upper mu 1 kokushibo  is destroyed genya and muichiro both die  from the wounds they suffered in the  battle against kokushibo but sanemy and  gyomay live long enough to fight in the  final battle against muzon unlike muzon  who completely abandoned his humanity in  the pursuit of power and immortality  kokushibo could never fully give up on  his human side despite making a deal  with the devil and despite betraying and  cutting down his own comrades he still  held on to his humanity he still saw  himself as a samurai who followed a code  of honor and proper etiquette he still  felt an attachment to his family which  is why he was so proud of muichiro and  he still felt a deep connection to his  brother yorichi even though a part of  him hated yurichi due to jealousy a part  of him still loved his brother and we  see proof of that when kokushiba's body  finally disintegrates and all that's  left is his clothing and the broken  flute that he had made for his brother  all those centuries ago kokushibo had  held on to that flute for literally  centuries just like he had held on to at  least some fragment of his humanity this  is why i love kokushibo as a character  yes he is incredibly strong and badass  yes he has a great design but he is also  a deeply flawed and in some ways  hypocritical character and in that sense  he is a deeply human character despite  being an overpowered demon who was  supposed to have abandoned his humanity  it is quite likely that even the team up  of three different hashira and genya  would not have been successful in taking  kukushibo down if he wasn't also faced  with a massive crisis of conscience at  the same time if kokushibo had been a  completely amoral sociopath like muzon  or doma he likely would have won the  fight against the demon slayers and  muzad would never have been defeated but  interestingly enough kokushibo was so  shocked by his own lack of humanity that  he couldn't keep fighting and so  ironically what was left of his humanity  was the very thing that ultimately led  to his defeat his defeat itself proved  that in the end kokushibo was still  human at least to some extent  i hope you guys enjoyed this video and  definitely let me know what you think of  kokushiba's character down in the  comments below if you're looking for a  video to watch next check out my  extensive breakdown of every upper demon  moon's death i will link it in the  description be sure to leave a quick  like and comment if you want to support  this video in that treacherous youtube  algorithm and if you're new here or you  watch our videos but you just haven't  taken the time to subscribe yet do me a  huge favor and make this the video that  you subscribe and hit that notification  bell to turn on all notifications it  seems like a small and unimportant thing  but actually subscribing really helps  out a lot on youtube you can also hit me  up on twitter and instagram at anime  uproar as always thank you guys so much  for watching and until next time see ya  space cowboys
 

